        back:   "## All Organisms Are Made of Cells\n\n**The first principle is that all organisms are composed of one or more cells, and the processes of metabolism and heredity occur within these cells.**\n\nThis principle is not just about structure; it is about function. The cell is where everything happens. If a process is part of life — breaking down food, making proteins, copying DNA — that process occurs inside a cell.\n\nAn organism might be a single cell, like a bacterium, or an assembly of trillions, like a human being. Either way, the cells are where the chemistry of life takes place.\n\n> **Key point:** For why the cell is called the functional unit of life, the answer involves metabolism and heredity occurring within it."
