        back:   "## The Vehicle of Heredity\n\n**A chromosome is an elongated cellular structure composed of DNA and protein that carries genetic information and transmits it from parent to offspring.**\n\nThe chromosome is the physical basis of heredity. Each chromosome carries a linear sequence of genes, and the collection of genes on all chromosomes constitutes the organism's genome. When a cell divides, each chromosome is replicated and one copy is delivered to each daughter cell, ensuring genetic continuity.\n\nChromosomes exist in two structural states. In a non-dividing cell, they form a diffuse network called chromatin. During cell division, they condense into the compact, visible structures recognised under the microscope.\n\nThe number of chromosomes is characteristic of a species but not of complexity. Humans have 46, fruit flies 8, and some ferns over 1000.\n\n> **Exam tip:** On the function of chromosomes, the answer involves carrying and transmitting genetic information."
