        back:   "## The Classic X-Linked Cross\n\n**Half of the sons are expected to be affected and half of the daughters are expected to be carriers; no daughter is affected.**\n\nThe cross is \\(X^A X^a \\times X^A Y\\). Daughters are \\(X^A X^A\\) (normal) or \\(X^A X^a\\) (carrier) in equal numbers. Sons are \\(X^A Y\\) (normal) or \\(X^a Y\\) (affected) in equal numbers.\n\nOverall, each of the four genotypes occurs with probability 1/4. So 1/4 of all children are affected sons, and 1/2 of sons are affected.\n\n> **Common trap:** 1/4 of all children are affected sons, but 1/2 of sons are affected. Read whether the question asks about all children or only sons."
