        back:   "## Father Affected, Mother Normal\n\n**All daughters are carriers and all sons are normal.**\n\nThe cross is \\(X^a Y \\times X^A X^A\\). Every daughter gets the father's \\(X^a\\) and the mother's \\(X^A\\), so all are carriers. Every son gets the father's Y and the mother's \\(X^A\\), so all are normal.\n\nThe trait skips a generation in the males and passes through the carrier daughters to their sons.\n\n> **Remember:** An affected father never gives an X-linked recessive trait to his sons. He gives it to his daughters, who become carriers."
