        back:   "## Mother Affected, Father Normal\n\n**All sons are affected and all daughters are carriers.**\n\nThe cross is \\(X^a X^a \\times X^A Y\\). Every son receives an \\(X^a\\) from the mother and a Y from the father, so every son is affected. Every daughter receives \\(X^a\\) from the mother and \\(X^A\\) from the father, so every daughter is a carrier.\n\nThis is the only common cross in which all sons of one family are affected.\n\n> **Exam tip:** An affected mother means all sons affected. This is the quickest way to recognise X-linked recessive inheritance in a pedigree."
