        back:   "## Multiply Down the Branches\n\n**The forked-line method gives the probability of each combined genotype or phenotype by multiplying the single-gene probabilities along each branch.**\n\nFor RrYy × RrYy, the first gene gives 3/4 round and 1/4 wrinkled. The second gives 3/4 yellow and 1/4 green. The four branches are round yellow (3/4 × 3/4 = 9/16), round green (3/16), wrinkled yellow (3/16) and wrinkled green (1/16).\n\nThis reproduces the 9:3:3:1 ratio without a 16-box square, and it extends easily to three or more genes.\n\n> **Exam tip:** Use the forked-line method for any cross of three or more genes. It is quicker and less error-prone than a Punnett square."
